Description: Wild OS sheet tabs, headings, status bar and zoom slider
 Tables' sheet tabs sit on the ribbon's tab row colour: the current sheet
 is a soft 26 px pill with an accent line along its foot and its name
 semibold, other sheets are quiet labels without rules between them, and
 sheet colours chosen by the user fill their pill. The scroll buttons only
 show while some sheets are out of sight. Tab bars elsewhere (layers in
 Draw) are drawn as before.
 Row and column headings and the corner are the paper's light grey with
 grey numbers, in light and dark mode alike, since the cells are white.
 The status bar is one band in the title bar's colour with its text in the
 quiet ink and no rules between fields or along its top, and the zoom
 slider is a 3 px track with an 11 px accent knob, as on the boards. The
 selection's figures in Tables' status bar start at their field's left
 edge rather than its middle.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

